        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.08750v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-07-09T17:50:07Z",
        "description": "Observations of debris discs have the potential to provide us with valuable information about massive planets perturbing them gravitationally. In this work, we explore the evolution of the azimuthally-averaged (or axisymmetric) surface density (ASD) -- a characteristic routinely derived from observa",
        "title_cn": "由长期行星扰动引起的碎片盘子结构"
      },
